To whom it may concern

I would like to know if there is a way of separating out the foreground and background spatial plots? I assume the spatial plots that are given as an example in the google.groups quality assessment of raw data section. I am using Gene ST 1.0 Human arrays.

Is there a way of creating a box plot representing the log2 probe intensities of each array on one box plot? As opposed to doing plotDensities for each array?

Also is there a way to analyse the individual probes as opposed to the probesets?

Thank you

--
Cathrine Mitchell

